nceptional folic acid consumption in The Netherlands from 1994 to 1995. Eur J Clin Pharmacol 54(4):329&#x02013;331 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9696958</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><label>13.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Robbins</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Cleves</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Collins</surname><given-names>HB</given-names></name><name><surname>Andrews</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>LN</given-names></name><name><surname>Hobbs</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Randomized trial of a physician-based intervention to increase the use of folic acid supplements among women</article-title><source>Am J Obstet Gynecol</source><year>2005</year><volume>192</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>1126</fpage><lpage>1132</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.ajog.2004.10.620</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Robbins JM, Cleves MA, Collins HB, Andrews N, Smith LN, Hobbs CA (2005) Randomized trial of a physician-based intervention to increase the use of folic acid supplements among women. Am J Obstet Gynecol 192(4):1126&#x02013;1132 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15846191</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jong&#x02013;van den Berg</surname><given-names>LT</given-names></name><name><surname>Hernandez&#x02013;Diaz</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Werler</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name><name><surname>Louik</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Mitchell</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Trends and predictors of folic acid awareness and periconceptional use in pregnant women</article-title><source>Am J Obstet Gynecol</source><year>2005</year><volume>192</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>121</fpage><lpage>128</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.ajog.2004.05.085</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">de Jong-van den Berg LT, Hernandez-Diaz S, Werler MM, Louik C, Mitchell AA (2005) Trends and predictors of folic acid awareness and periconceptional use in pregnant women. Am J Obstet Gynecol 192(1):121&#x02013;128 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15672013</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eichholzer</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Tonz</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Zimmermann</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Folic acid: a public-health challenge</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>2006</year><volume>367</volume><issue>9519</issue><fpage>1352</fpage><lpage>1361</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0140-6736(06)68582-6</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Eichholzer M, Tonz O, Zimmermann R (2006) Folic acid: a public-health challenge. Lancet 367(9519):1352&#x02013;1361 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16631914</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>